:"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-02-08T11:15:08Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T15:43:08Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.6.0.stable, 4.5.1.stable, 4.4.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon 780M (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.22029.9039) - AMD Ryzen 7 7840HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads) - 15.29 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n\nWhen my system scaling is set to 100%, it works fine.\nBut when adjusted to 200% scaling, the cropped area's side length shrinks to 50% of what is displayed in the workspace.\n\nSystem 100% Scale:\n<img width=\"2880\" height=\"1760\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e46208b9-4287-4fe7-a884-ede2ad7a73b5\" />\n\nSystem 200% Scale:\n<img width=\"2880\" height=\"1720\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1822dbcc-e681-429e-b814-7482689a28e4\" />\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Set system scaling to 100%, open the project, run the project, and obtain normal results.\n\n2. Close the entire Godot program.\n\n3. Adjust system scaling to 200%, reopen the project, and run it to obtain abnormal results.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[pppaint.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25160707/pppaint.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116043/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116043/timel